From: mscharged-port
Subject: Rollback: a replay draws nothing
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

A rollback replays whole frames, GameRenderTask included, so that the
presentation it took back with the match (the darkening after a goal, the
indicators, the blinks, the frame lock, the goal replay that
RenderSnapshotAt starts) follows the match again. The drawing ran too and
went nowhere, as GLView drops what a replay attaches: 1.3 ms of every
replayed frame, a third of it.

During a replay (mscharged_rollback_resimulating) the drawing task now
skips what only draws: RenderSnapshot::Render's characters, objects,
power-ups, ball and nets, the world NPCs, the flares, the warble, the
darkening, the shadow volumes and the score numbers. What updates still
runs, the calls that update and draw as one included: the hidden actors'
timer, the camera's up vector and the goal light in RenderSnapshot::Render,
Blend (the stadium's animation, the goal light's and the goalie nets'
state), the warble, the darkening and every other update of
GameRenderTask. The picture in picture is left alone: it plays in the goal
replays, which no rollback reaches.

The characters' skin meshes then keep the poses of their last drawing
after a replay: the simulation poses the characters with their own pose
accumulators, the skin meshes only feed the drawing, and the next drawing
poses them again. With a rollback every step, every replayed checksum was
the first run's; the drawing task's replay went from 1320 to 669 us a
frame, a rollback from 13.1 to 10.7 ms on average.

